3. Modifications to src/solver/ (DistQLDPC patches)
-----------------------------------------------------

Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Yu-Fang Chen <yfc@iis.sinica.edu.tw>
Part of DistQLDPC (GPL-3.0-or-later when distributed as this project).

These changes are documented in detail in MODIFICATIONS.md. Summary:

  - Bounds pipe API (TRY / LB / UB messages for parent-process progress)
  - Best-solution tracking and printing on timeout / interrupt
  - Configurable cardinality encoding modes (Sinz / MTO / off)
  - Retire inactive unit and auxiliary soft literals after preprocessing
    partition, preserving representative clauses and objective accounting (GH58)
  - Multi-instance search controls and per-instance heuristic state (interleaved CSS split, experimental)

Modified files (partial list): Solver.h, Solver.cc

  src/core/distqldpc.cc also contains GH-85 per-half symmetry breaking
  (GH-73 x GH-75 interaction): an original, domain-specific adaptation of
  static symmetry breaking (Crawford et al., KR 1996; Anders, Brenner, Rattan,
  "Satsuma", SAT 2024, DOI 10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.4). No third-party code.
  src/core/distqldpc.cc also contains GH-87 dual-half elimination (an
  original use of verified XZ-dual qubit permutations to prove dX = dZ in
  the GH-73 split; GF(2) checks reused from GH-75). No third-party code.

The original MaxCDCL engine remains under MIT. All upstream copyright
and permission notices in src/solver/ must be preserved in copies and
substantial portions, per the MIT license.


